## 3. PROV-04 rationale

PROV-04 is **Financing integrity**: controls over receivables, inventory finance and collateral. It has the most direct documented credit link in the findings. Alleged double-pledged collateral and undisclosed off-balance-sheet financing at Tricolor and First Brands led to sudden insolvency and to disclosed bank losses: JPMorgan $170m and Fifth Third $200m [S-061, S-062, S-066, S-067].
The other sector-specific candidates were not selected. Restart capability for plant IT and operational technology (IT/OT) is already covered by PROV-02 (Recovery testing). Controls against payment diversion through business email compromise (BEC) rest on one historical case, Toyota Boshoku in 2019 [S-073].

